blic  blockchains which have complete  transparency disparity like these will  become evident moreover there is an  issue with regards to competition all  banks are competing with each other in  order to create a better place for  themselves in the market thus they want  their confidential information about  transactions and other operations to  stay completely confidential this won't  be possible in a public blockchain like  aetherium which stores all smart  contracts on public Ledger's this is  where platforms like hyper ledger come  into the picture which permits  permissioned and private transactions  and it is highly scalable as a platform  solution to the restrictions on hyper  ledger network only parties directly  related to the transaction deal are  updated on the ledger thus maintaining  privacy and confidentiality hyper ledger  primarily leverages the concept of  channels to ensure privacy and  confidentiality  a channel is basically a virtual  blockchain network which sits atop a  physical blockchain network and has its  own access rules they employed their own  mechanism for transaction ordering and  thus ensure scalability thereby  permitting effective ordering along with  the separation of data in the above  example when John and Kat are conducting  a transaction a private channel between  them serves as a method of interaction  the smart contract can thus be viewed by  only these two parties and the network's  endorsement policy verifies their  membership with the network to ensure  privacy  thus the transaction is secure and  private and confidential hyper ledger  transaction in the above example John is  initiating a transaction to send a  message to Kat let's assume that we have  a state in the ledger named as message  denoting the last message that had been  sent and its store as a key value here  in peer of organisation now John has  decided to send a new message to Kat and  submit a request to the nodejs back-end  from the message dashboard the 