ogic one of the examples where it is  used is fishing industry to track the  supply chain of fishes burrow hyper  ledger burrow hosted by the Linux  Foundation is a blockchain framework  implementation the framework was  contributed by Monde ax &amp; Co sponsored  by Intel Borough is a permission smart  contract application engine partially  developed in accordance to the  specifications of aetherium virtual  machine EVM  it is used to run etherium smart  contracts Iroha hyper ledger  Iroha hosted by the linux foundation is  another blockchain platform  implementation the framework was  contributed by Sora Mitsui Hitachi  NTT DATA in colu written in C++ hyper  ledger  Aroha incorporates a unique algorithm on  chain based Byzantine fault tolerant  consensus it provides a small set of  fast commands and queries covering most  common operations for the digital asset  and Identity Management it can be used  in mobile application organization  indeed hyper ledger  in D is a distributed ledger and utility  library built for decentralized identity  the distributed ledger provides tools  libraries and reusable components to  create and use independent digital  identities based on block chains they  are inoperable across administrative  applications domains and any other silo  it is used as a decentralized identity  database Sawtooth hyper ledger Sawtooth  is a blockchain platform built for  enterprise use where the design focuses  on maintaining the safety of smart  contract and the Ledger's are kept  distributed sawtooth offers a simplified  platform for blockchain application  development by separating the  application domain at the core system  level application developers could opt  for a language of their choice to write  smart contracts logic following are some  of the key features of sawtooth  application layer in core system  separation parallel transaction  execution pluggable consensus algorithm  private networks with sawtooth  permissioning features aetherium  contract compatible with seth event  system hyper ledger architecture hyper  ledger blockchain network participants  following are the  front participants within hyper ledger  blockchain blockchain user a blockchain  user performs transaction on the network  the user can invoke a function from the  chain code in order to send the  instruction message to the underlying  network which can then process the  transaction certificate authority  certificate authority ensures that only  certain restricted parties can be a part  of the business network on hyper ledger  they access security certifications in  order to determine the parties who have  required privileges to be an actor on a  network traditional database it is a  standard database which is used to store  data traditional processing platform  it stores access to the logical code  written which is used to run the network  as per the design blockchain development  network it operates the blockchain  network which enables the execution of  smart contracts chain code as well as  various transactions that take place  between the participants which are part  of the network blockchain developer a  developer develops applications on the  blockchain using chain code currently  hyper ledger fabric supports node.js  Java and golang languages to write such  chain codes  regulator regulator runs oversight to  ensure that the platform is operating  without any bias hyper ledger  architecture following are three main  components of hyper ledger membership  service it is a set of cryptographic  materials certificates that defines  organization by itself every peer in  order needs this type of certificate  this certificate has some common  property by which we decide whether the  pier and the orderer  belongs to the same organization or not  a pier which is a part of the same MSP  can communicate with each other a pier  from other organizations cannot be  allowed to communicate with each other  blockchain and transaction layer this  layer constitutes the core code of the  blockchain it comprises of consensus  algorithm which is required to make the  final decision  on the state of every transaction it  also contains the distributed ledger and  ledger storage which stores the entire  history of the transactions and the  last-known States lastly we have the p2p  protocol which is used for communication  between different nodes on the network  chain code it is the logical programming  layer which consists of the business  logic required to run in operation on  the hyper listen'd blockchain and it's  consensus model permissioned blockchain  maintains an access control layer and  allows certain actions to be performed  only by a few identifiable participants  it is also called private blockchain  following are the properties specific to  permission to block chains it has  legally accountable validators it is  suitable for off chain assets they can  be used as an IT tool for settlement and  clearing examples include ripple which  determines roles for a select number of  participants who can act as transaction  validators on their network such block  chains are also popular among industry  level enterprises and businesses  for which security identity and role  definition are important permissioned  versus permissionless blockchain let us  see some differences between a  permission and a permission list  blockchain one in regards to access a  permissioned blockchain only allows  pre-approved members to access the  network and make transactions to it  whereas a permission list blockchain  allows anyone to be a part of the  network as it is completely open and  transparent to permissioned blockchain  are faster than permission list  blockchain when it comes to performance  as they have less number of participants  in the network 3 permissioned blockchain  use different types of consensus  algorithms like pbft proof of stake and  more usually permissionless block chains  rely on proof of work for the  transaction cost in a permissioned  blockchain is lower than that of a  permission list blockchain 5 in regards  to stability permissioned blockchain are  considered more stable compared to  permissionless block chains as the  former have a better governance due to  known parties which are a part of the  network six in a permissionless  blockchain all participants have the  same level of access where as a  permission blockchain provides full  access only to the members which are  registered to be a part of the business  network 7 permission lists block chains  work in a peer-to-peer fashion relying  solely on consensus algorithms to create  a trusted environment however  permissioned block chains have trusted  members as part of the network which  enhances the trust on the network  consensus and it's interaction with  architectural layers consensus consensus  is the process by which a network of  nodes validates the block of  transactions and provide a guaranteed  ordering of transactions and validating  those block of transactions that  to be committed to the ledger consensus  must ensure the following in the network  confirms the correctness of all  transactions in a proposed block  according to endorsement and Consensus  policies agrees on an order and  correctness and hints on the results of  execution depends on smart contract  layer to verify correctness of an  ordered set of transactions in a block  hyper ledger it makes use of the  permissioned voting base consensus from  the pool of the other consensus named  the lottery based consensus consensus  properties consensus must satisfy two  properties to guarantee agreement among  nodes safety and liveness safety means  that each node is guaranteed the same  sequence of inputs and results in the  same output on each node the algorithm  must behave identical to a single node  system that executes each transaction  atomically one at a time  liveness means that each non faulty node  will eventually receive every submitted  transaction assuming that communication  does not fail activities performed to  reach consensus hyper ledger frameworks  reach consensus by performing two  activities transaction or during  transaction validation biologically  separating these activities we ensure  that any hyper ledger framework can work  with any hyper ledger consensus module  the first step of the consensus process  flow is receiving the transactions from  the client application consensus depends  on an ordering service to order  transactions transaction order enables  confidentiality of the transactions it  also increases the efficiency of the  transactions to validate transactions  consensus depends on the smart contract  layer because it contains the business  logic behind what makes a transaction  valid  transaction validation contains business  logic to make the transaction valid it  also ensures the confirmation of  policies and contracts specified for the  transaction then it also checks for  syntax and logic errors consensus model  for permissioned blockchain consensus in  hyper ledger fabric as seen in the image  above is broken out into three phases  endorsement ordering and validation  endorsement is driven by policy eg M out  of n signatures upon which participants  endorse a transaction or during phase  accepts the endorsed transactions and  agrees to the order to be committed on  the ledger validation takes a block of  ordered transactions and validates the  correctness of the results including  checking endorsement policy and double  spending as soon as a new transaction is  created it is sent to the endorsement  peer to generate a readwrite pair the  readwrite pair from every endorser is  then sent to the order ur which orders  the same and generates a block based on  consensus the ordered block is then sent  to the validator to update the couch DB  with the most recent state API and  network topology in hyper ledger API it  enables clients and applications to  interface to the blockchains hyper  ledger supports the following types of  AP is admin ap is this class creates an  administration connection to a hyper  ledger composer runtime the connection  can then be used to deploy Business  Network definitions undeploy business  network definitions update business  network definitions send a ping message  to the runtime to ensure it is running  and correctly configured  story connection profile document in the  connection profile store common api's  they are used to obtain information  about the connected networks this  information can include business network  metadata enum declaration and many more  run-time api's these are used to perform  all transaction operations like running  a query managing assets and more network  topology network topology is a technical  infrastructure that provides smart  contract services and ledger to  applications listed below are the  components of network topology ledger a  leisure consists of two distinct parts a  blockchain and the state database  unlike other Ledger's blockchains are  immutable  in contrast the world state is a  database containing the current value of  the set of key value pairs that have  been added modified or deleted by the  set of validated and committed  transactions in the blockchain smart  contract a smart contract is a code that  is invoked by a client application  external to the blockchain network it  manages access and modifications to a  set of key value pairs in the world  state in hyper ledger fabric smart  contracts are referred to as a chain  code peer nodes it is a network entity  that maintains a ledger and runs chain  code containers in order to perform  read/write operations to the ledger  peers are owned and maintained by  members or during service it is a  defined collective of nodes that orders  transactions into a block the ordering  service exists independent of the peer  processes and orders transactions on a  first-come first-served basis for all  channels on the network channels a  channel is a private blockchain overlay  which allows for data isolation and  confidentiality a channel specific  ledger is shared across the peers in the  channel and transacting parties must be  properly authenticated to a channel in  order to interact with it fabric  certificate authorities hyper ledger  fabric CA is the default certificate  authority component which issues PKI  based search  tickets to network member organizations  and their users the CA issues one root  certificate to each member and one  enrollment certificate to each  authorized user steps to create a hyper  letter following steps should be  followed to create a hyperlink network  is created from the definition of the  consortium including its clients peers  channels and ordering service the  ordering service is the administration  point for the network because it  contains the configuration for the  channel within the network step to  define a consortium a consortium is  comprised of two or more organizations  on the network consortiums are defined  by organizations that have a need for  transacting business with one another  and they must agree to the policies that  govern the network step 3  create a channel for consortium a  channel is a means of communication used  to connect the components of the network  and or the member client applications  step 4 join peers to channels peers are  joined to channels by the organizations  that own them and there can be multiple  peer nodes on channels within the  network  step 5 install smart contracts smart  contract chain code must be installed  and instantiated on a peer in order for  a client application to be able to  invoke the smart contract step 6  optimize the network while there is no  theoretical limit on how big a network  can get as the network grows it is  important to consider design choices  that will help optimize network  throughput stability and resilience step  7  add another consortium definition as  consortium are defined and is added to  the existing channel we must update the  channel configuration by sending a  channel configuration update transaction  to the  or during service step 8 add a new  channel organizations are what form and  join channels and channel configurations  can be amended to add organizations as  the network grows when adding a new  channel to the network channel policies  remain separate from other channels  configured on the same network step 9  add peer and join it to multiple  channels you can continue adding new  peers and connect them to several  channels within the network network  topology the diagram above shows a that  network with the following configuration  there is a fabric network in with  network policy np-1 and ordering service  o channel c1 is governed by channel  policy CP 1 channel c1 has been  established by consortium RA RB channel  c1 is managed by ordering service o and  peers p1 and p2 and client applications  a1 and a2 have been granted permission  to transact on c1 client application a 1  is owned by organization are a  certificate authority CA 1 serves  organization are a peer P 2 maintains  Leger l1 associated with channel C 1 and  L 2 associated with C 2  P R P to makes use of chain code s4 and  s5 the order nodes of ordering service o  are owned by organization Rd hi there if  you like this video subscribe to the  simply learn youtube channel and click  here to watch similar videos to nerd up  and get certified click here

